{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"/*\\n * This code was based on Sokoban C available at\\n * http://www.rosettacode.org/wiki/Sokoban#C\\n * licenced under GNU Free Documentation License 1.2\\n */\\n\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <unistd.h>\\n#include <stdint.h>\\n#include <assert.h>\\n#include <stdbool.h>\\n\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#include <omp.h>\\n#endif\\n\\nint w, h, n_boxes;\\nuint8_t * board, * goals, * live;\\n\\ntypedef uint16_t cidx_t;\\ntypedef uint32_t hash_t;\\n\\n/* board configuration is represented by an array of cell indices\\n   of player and boxes */\\ntypedef struct state_t state_t;\\n\\nstruct state_t { // variable length\\n    hash_t h;\\n    state_t * prev, * next, * qnext;\\n    cidx_t c[];\\n};\\n\\nsize_t state_size, block_size = 32;\\nstate_t * block_root, * block_head;\\n\\ninline\\nstate_t * newstate(state_t * parent) {\\n    inline state_t * next_of(state_t * s) {\\n        return (void * )((uint8_t * ) s + state_size);\\n    }\\n\\n    state_t * ptr;\\n    if (!block_head) {\\n        block_size *= 2;\\n        state_t * p = malloc(block_size * state_size);\\n        assert(p);\\n        p -> next = block_root;\\n        block_root = p;\\n        ptr = (void * )((uint8_t * ) p + state_size * block_size);\\n        p = block_head = next_of(p);\\n        state_t * q;\\n        for (q = next_of(p); q < ptr; p = q, q = next_of(q))\\n            p -> next = q;\\n        p -> next = NULL;\\n    }\\n\\n    ptr = block_head;\\n    block_head = block_head -> next;\\n\\n    ptr -> prev = parent;\\n    ptr -> h = 0;\\n    return ptr;\\n}\\n\\ninline\\nvoid unnewstate(state_t * p) {\\n    p -> next = block_head;\\n    block_head = p;\\n}\\n\\nenum {\\n    space,\\n    wall,\\n    player,\\n    box\\n};\\n\\n// mark up positions where a box definitely should not be\\nvoid mark_live(const int c) {\\n    const int y = c / w,\\n        x = c % w;\\n    if (live[c]) return;\\n\\n    live[c] = 1;\\n    if (y > 1 && board[c - w] != wall && board[c - w * 2] != wall)\\n        mark_live(c - w);\\n    if (y < h - 2 && board[c + w] != wall && board[c + w * 2] != wall)\\n        mark_live(c + w);\\n    if (x > 1 && board[c - 1] != wall && board[c - 2] != wall)\\n        mark_live(c - 1);\\n    if (x < w - 2 && board[c + 1] != wall && board[c + 2] != wall)\\n        mark_live(c + 1);\\n}\\n\\nstate_t * parse_board(const char * s) {\\n    board = calloc(w * h, sizeof(uint8_t));\\n    assert(board);\\n    goals = calloc(w * h, sizeof(uint8_t));\\n    assert(goals);\\n    live = calloc(w * h, sizeof(uint8_t));\\n    assert(live);\\n\\n    n_boxes = 0;\\n    for (int i = 0; s[i]; i++) {\\n        switch (s[i]) {\\n        case '#':\\n            board[i] = wall;\\n            continue;\\n\\n        case '.': // fallthrough\\n        case '+':\\n            goals[i] = 1; // fallthrough\\n        case '@':\\n            continue;\\n\\n        case '*':\\n            goals[i] = 1; // fallthrough\\n        case '$':\\n            n_boxes++;\\n            continue;\\n        default:\\n            continue;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    const int is = sizeof(int);\\n    state_size = (sizeof(state_t) + (1 + n_boxes) * sizeof(cidx_t) + is - 1) /\\n        is * is;\\n\\n    state_t * state = newstate(NULL);\\n\\n    for (int i = 0, j = 0; i < w * h; i++) {\\n        if (goals[i]) mark_live(i);\\n        if (s[i] == '$' || s[i] == '*')\\n            state -> c[++j] = i;\\n        else if (s[i] == '@' || s[i] == '+')\\n            state -> c[0] = i;\\n    }\\n\\n    return state;\\n}\\n\\n// K&R hash function\\ninline\\nvoid hash(state_t * s) {\\n    if (!s -> h) {\\n        register hash_t ha = 0;\\n        cidx_t * p = s -> c;\\n        for (int i = 0; i <= n_boxes; i++)\\n            ha = p[i] + 31 * ha;\\n        s -> h = ha;\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nstate_t ** buckets;\\nhash_t hash_size, fill_limit, filled;\\n\\nvoid extend_table() {\\n    int old_size = hash_size;\\n\\n    if (!old_size) {\\n        hash_size = 1024;\\n        filled = 0;\\n        fill_limit = hash_size * 3 / 4; // 0.75 load factor\\n    } else {\\n        hash_size *= 2;\\n        fill_limit *= 2;\\n    }\\n\\n    buckets = realloc(buckets, sizeof(state_t * ) * hash_size);\\n    assert(buckets);\\n\\n    // rehash\\n    memset(buckets + old_size, 0, sizeof(state_t * ) * (hash_size - old_size));\\n\\n    const hash_t bits = hash_size - 1;\\n    for (int i = 0; i < old_size; i++) {\\n        state_t * head = buckets[i];\\n        buckets[i] = NULL;\\n        while (head) {\\n            state_t * next = head -> next;\\n            const int j = head -> h & bits;\\n            head -> next = buckets[j];\\n            buckets[j] = head;\\n            head = next;\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nstate_t * lookup(state_t * s) {\\n    hash(s);\\n    state_t * f = buckets[s -> h & (hash_size - 1)];\\n    for (; f; f = f -> next) {\\n        if ( //(f->h == s->h) &&\\n            !memcmp(s -> c, f -> c, sizeof(cidx_t) * (1 + n_boxes)))\\n            break;\\n    }\\n\\n    return f;\\n}\\n\\nbool add_to_table(state_t * s) {\\n    if (lookup(s)) {\\n        unnewstate(s);\\n        return false;\\n    }\\n\\n    if (filled++ >= fill_limit)\\n        extend_table();\\n\\n    hash_t i = s -> h & (hash_size - 1);\\n\\n    s -> next = buckets[i];\\n    buckets[i] = s;\\n    return true;\\n}\\n\\nbool success(const state_t * s) {\\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n_boxes; i++)\\n        if (!goals[s -> c[i]]) return false;\\n    return true;\\n}\\n\\nstate_t * move_me(state_t * s,\\n    const int dy,\\n        const int dx) {\\n    const int y = s -> c[0] / w;\\n    const int x = s -> c[0] % w;\\n    const int y1 = y + dy;\\n    const int x1 = x + dx;\\n\\n    if (y1 < 0 || y1 >= h || x1 < 0 || x1 >= w)\\n        return NULL;\\n\\n    const int c1 = y1 * w + x1;\\n    if (board[c1] == wall)\\n        return NULL;\\n\\n    int at_box = 0;\\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n_boxes; i++) {\\n        if (s -> c[i] == c1) {\\n            at_box = i;\\n            break;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    int c2;\\n    if (at_box) {\\n        const int y2 = y1 + dy;\\n        const int x2 = x1 + dx;\\n        if (y2 < 0 || y2 >= h || x2 < 0 || x2 >= w)\\n            return NULL;\\n        c2 = y2 * w + x2;\\n        if (board[c2] == wall || !live[c2])\\n            return NULL;\\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n_boxes; i++)\\n            if (s -> c[i] == c2) return NULL;\\n    }\\n\\n    state_t * n;\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#pragma omp critical(sokoban_state_pool)\\n#endif\\n    n = newstate(s);\\n    memcpy(n -> c + 1, s -> c + 1, sizeof(cidx_t) * n_boxes);\\n\\n    cidx_t * p = n -> c;\\n    p[0] = c1;\\n\\n    if (at_box) p[at_box] = c2;\\n\\n    // leet bubble sort\\n    for (int i = n_boxes; --i;) {\\n        cidx_t t = 0;\\n        for (int j = 1; j < i; j++) {\\n            if (p[j] > p[j + 1])\\n                t = p[j], p[j] = p[j + 1], p[j + 1] = t;\\n        }\\n        if (!t) break;\\n    }\\n\\n    return n;\\n}\\n\\nstatic void append_candidate(state_t ** head, state_t ** tail,\\n    state_t * candidate) {\\n    candidate -> qnext = NULL;\\n    if (*tail)\\n        (*tail) -> qnext = candidate;\\n    else\\n        *head = candidate;\\n    *tail = candidate;\\n}\\n\\nstate_t * next_level, * done;\\n\\nbool queue_move(state_t * s) {\\n    if (!s || !add_to_table(s))\\n        return false;\\n\\n    if (success(s)) {\\n        done = s;\\n        return true;\\n    }\\n\\n    s -> qnext = next_level;\\n    next_level = s;\\n    return false;\\n}\\n\\nbool do_move(state_t * s) {\\n    return queue_move(move_me(s, 0, 1)) ||\\n        queue_move(move_me(s, 0, -1)) ||\\n        queue_move(move_me(s, -1, 0)) ||\\n        queue_move(move_me(s, 1, 0));\\n}\\n\\nvoid show_moves(const state_t * s, int nextPos) {\\n    if (s -> prev)\\n        show_moves(s -> prev, s -> c[0]);\\n    if (nextPos == -1) {\\n        printf(\\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n        return;\\n    }\\n    int cx = s -> c[0] % w;\\n    int cy = s -> c[0] / w;\\n    int nx = nextPos % w;\\n    int ny = nextPos / w;\\n    int box = 0;\\n    for (int i = 1; !box && i <= n_boxes; i++)\\n        box = s -> c[i] == nextPos;\\n    if (cx < nx) printf(box ? \\\"R\\\" : \\\"r\\\");\\n    else if (cx > nx) printf(box ? \\\"L\\\" : \\\"l\\\");\\n    else if (cy < ny) printf(box ? \\\"D\\\" : \\\"d\\\");\\n    else if (cy > ny) printf(box ? \\\"U\\\" : \\\"u\\\");\\n    else if (1) {\\n        printf(\\\"Invalid move\\\\n\\\");\\n        exit(1);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n    size_t sz = 1024;\\n    char * boardStr = malloc(sz * sizeof(char));\\n    char * pos = boardStr;\\n    w = -1;\\n    h = 0;\\n    while (1) {\\n        int read = getline( & pos, & sz, stdin);\\n        if (read == -1) break;\\n        if (read >= w) w = read;\\n        sz -= read;\\n        pos += read;\\n        h++;\\n    }\\n    state_t * s = parse_board(boardStr);\\n    free(boardStr);\\n\\n    extend_table();\\n    queue_move(s);\\n\\n    int use_parallel = 0;\\n    state_t ** thread_heads = NULL;\\n    state_t ** thread_tails = NULL;\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n    int max_threads = omp_get_max_threads();\\n    if (max_threads > 1) {\\n        thread_heads = calloc((size_t) max_threads, sizeof(*thread_heads));\\n        thread_tails = calloc((size_t) max_threads, sizeof(*thread_tails));\\n        if (thread_heads && thread_tails) {\\n            use_parallel = 1;\\n        } else {\\n            free(thread_heads);\\n            free(thread_tails);\\n            thread_heads = NULL;\\n            thread_tails = NULL;\\n        }\\n    }\\n#endif\\n\\n    bool no_solution = false;\\n\\n    /* Keep small searches entirely sequential so they pay no team startup cost. */\\n    while (!done) {\\n        state_t * head = next_level;\\n        size_t frontier_count = 0;\\n        for (state_t * p = head; p; p = p -> qnext)\\n            frontier_count++;\\n\\n        if (use_parallel && frontier_count >= 32)\\n            break;\\n\\n        next_level = NULL;\\n        for (; head && !done; head = head -> qnext)\\n            do_move(head);\\n\\n        if (!next_level && !done) {\\n            no_solution = true;\\n            break;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    if (use_parallel && !done && !no_solution) {\\n        state_t * frontier_head = NULL;\\n        size_t frontier_count = 0;\\n        int team_size = 1;\\n        int parallel_expand = 0;\\n        int stop = 0;\\n\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#pragma omp parallel default(shared)\\n#endif\\n        {\\n            state_t * local_head = NULL;\\n            state_t * local_tail = NULL;\\n\\n            while (1) {\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#pragma omp single\\n#endif\\n                {\\n                    if (done) {\\n                        stop = 1;\\n                    } else if (!next_level) {\\n                        no_solution = true;\\n                        stop = 1;\\n                    } else {\\n                        stop = 0;\\n                        frontier_head = next_level;\\n                        next_level = NULL;\\n                        frontier_count = 0;\\n                        for (state_t * p = frontier_head; p; p = p -> qnext)\\n                            frontier_count++;\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n                        team_size = omp_get_num_threads();\\n#else\\n                        team_size = 1;\\n#endif\\n                        parallel_expand = team_size > 1 &&\\n                            thread_heads != NULL && thread_tails != NULL &&\\n                            frontier_count >= 32;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n\\n                if (stop)\\n                    break;\\n\\n                local_head = NULL;\\n                local_tail = NULL;\\n                if (parallel_expand) {\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n                    const int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\\n#else\\n                    const int tid = 0;\\n#endif\\n                    const size_t id = (size_t) tid;\\n                    const size_t nthreads = (size_t) team_size;\\n                    const size_t base = frontier_count / nthreads;\\n                    const size_t extra = frontier_count % nthreads;\\n                    const size_t begin = base * id + (id < extra ? id : extra);\\n                    const size_t end = begin + base + (id < extra);\\n                    state_t * parent = frontier_head;\\n                    for (size_t i = 0; i < begin; i++)\\n                        parent = parent -> qnext;\\n\\n                    for (size_t i = begin; i < end; i++, parent = parent -> qnext) {\\n                        append_candidate(&local_head, &local_tail,\\n                            move_me(parent, 0, 1));\\n                        append_candidate(&local_head, &local_tail,\\n                            move_me(parent, 0, -1));\\n                        append_candidate(&local_head, &local_tail,\\n                            move_me(parent, -1, 0));\\n                        append_candidate(&local_head, &local_tail,\\n                            move_me(parent, 1, 0));\\n                    }\\n                    thread_heads[tid] = local_head;\\n                    thread_tails[tid] = local_tail;\\n                } else {\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#pragma omp single\\n#endif\\n                    {\\n                        for (state_t * head = frontier_head;\\n                            head && !done; head = head -> qnext)\\n                            do_move(head);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#pragma omp barrier\\n#endif\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#pragma omp single\\n#endif\\n                {\\n                    if (parallel_expand) {\\n                        for (int tid = 0; tid < team_size; tid++) {\\n                            state_t * candidate = thread_heads[tid];\\n                            thread_heads[tid] = NULL;\\n                            thread_tails[tid] = NULL;\\n                            while (candidate) {\\n                                state_t * next = candidate -> qnext;\\n                                if (done)\\n                                    unnewstate(candidate);\\n                                else\\n                                    queue_move(candidate);\\n                                candidate = next;\\n                            }\\n                        }\\n                    }\\n\\n                    if (done) {\\n                        stop = 1;\\n                    } else if (!next_level) {\\n                        no_solution = true;\\n                        stop = 1;\\n                    } else {\\n                        stop = 0;\\n                    }\\n                }\\n\\n                if (stop)\\n                    break;\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    free(thread_heads);\\n    free(thread_tails);\\n\\n    if (no_solution) {\\n        puts(\\\"no solution?\\\");\\n        return 1;\\n    }\\n\\n    show_moves(done, -1);\\n\\n    free(buckets);\\n    free(board);\\n    free(goals);\\n    free(live);\\n\\n    while (block_root) {\\n        void * tmp = block_root -> next;\\n        free(block_root);\\n        block_root = tmp;\\n    }\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/sokoban.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"A persistent OpenMP team, entered only when the BFS frontier reaches 32 states, can amortize per-layer team startup and speed wide layers on four cores. Contiguous static parent ranges and serial candidate merging in the existing parent/direction order preserve deterministic duplicate handling and solution tie-breaking.\",\"notes\":\"No commands or measurements were run. Parallel move generation protects the shared state pool; hash-table operations and ordered merging remain serial. The move bounds checks prevent speculative parallel generation from reading outside the board.\",\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Keep the small-frontier search sequential, then use one persistent OpenMP team to share wide BFS frontiers across contiguous parent ranges.\",\"Collect each worker's candidates in order and merge them serially by thread range, retaining the original expansion and tie-break order.\",\"Guard state-pool allocation in parallel move generation and reject moves that leave board bounds.\"]}"}}
